\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{Block means share one mass}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Fix an integer #{B\ge 1}, a mass #{\mu>0}, and a
\vocabk{finite-range circle precision}{fdip-00C8} with
second-order coefficient #{\kappa}. Let #{N=BM} with
#{M\ge 1} and #{N>2R}, and let #{\varphi} be the rescaled
field of \ref{fdip-00CB}. Write #{A_b} for the mean of the
#{M} consecutive coordinates of #{\varphi} on the
half-open interval from #{b/B} to #{(b+1)/B}. These are
the means in the \vocabk{block averages}{fdip-00BL}, applied
to #{\varphi}. As #{M\to\infty}, the covariance operator of
#{(A_0,\ldots,A_{B-1})} on the real counting space of the
#{B} block labels converges to the covariance operator of
\ref{fdip-00BO} at mass squared
#{m^2=\frac{\mu}{\kappa}}. That operator commutes with the
cyclic shift of the block labels. Its canonical kernel is
#{C(b,c)=\mathbb E(A_bA_c)}.}

\proof{
\p{Let #{h} be the counting inner product on the residues
modulo #{N}. Declare the counting basis of site indicators.
The counting covariance operator of #{\varphi} is
#{\kappa N Q_N^{-1}}. In that basis the pairing
#{h(\delta_u,(\kappa N Q_N^{-1})\delta_v)} is the kernel
##{\mathbb E\bigl(\varphi(u)\varphi(v)\bigr)
=\kappa\sum_{p=0}^{N-1}\lambda_p^{-1}
\exp\bigl(2\pi i p(u-v)/N\bigr),}
where #{\lambda_p=\mu+N^2\alpha(2\pi p/N)}. The geometric sum
over a block is the one in the proof of \ref{fdip-00BO}, and
it contributes the same ratio of sines. Hence
##{\mathbb E(A_bA_c)
=\sum_{p=0}^{N-1}t_{N,p}
\exp\bigl(2\pi i p(b-c)/B\bigr).}
The constant mode contributes #{t_{N,0}=\frac{\kappa}{\mu}}.
For
every other mode,
##{t_{N,p}=\frac{\kappa B^2\sin^2(\pi p/B)}
{N^2\sin^2(\pi p/N)\,\lambda_p}.}}
\p{Take the representative of #{p} in a symmetric range of
length #{N}. The chord bound in the proof of \ref{fdip-00BO}
gives #{\sin(\pi |p|/N)\ge 2|p|/N} for #{1\le |p|\le N/2}, so
#{N^2\sin^2(\pi p/N)\ge 4p^2}. Since #{\lambda_p\ge\mu} and
the squared sine in the numerator is at most #{1},
##{t_{N,p}\le\frac{\kappa B^2}{4\mu p^2}.}
Extend #{t_{N,p}} by zero outside that range. For each fixed
#{p\ne 0}, the mode computation of \ref{fdip-00CC} gives
#{N^2\alpha(2\pi p/N)\to 4\pi^2\kappa p^2} and
#{N\sin(\pi p/N)\to\pi p}, so
##{t_{N,p}\to
\frac{B^2\sin^2(\pi p/B)}
{(\pi p)^2\bigl(m^2+(2\pi p)^2\bigr)}.}
The comparison #{\kappa B^2/(4\mu p^2)} is summable over the
nonzero integers and does not depend on #{N}. Split the sum
into the terms with #{|p|\le P} and the tail. The tail is
smaller than any prescribed positive tolerance, uniformly in
#{N}, once #{P} is large. Each of the finitely many remaining
terms converges. The resulting kernel is the canonical
kernel of the covariance operator of \ref{fdip-00BO} at mass
squared #{m^2}.}
}
